[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m Find the largest possible real part of \[(75+117i)z+\frac{96+144i}{z}\]where $z$ is a complex number with $|z|=4$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m Remember to put your answer on its own line after "Answer:".
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m First, we substitute \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i) \cdot 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m = 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m Now, we combine these two parts:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m = (300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(300\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta + 36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m = (324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta) + i(336\cos\theta + 276\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we can use the fact that the maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -432\), so the maximum value is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + (-432)^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(\boxed{540}\).
