[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we need to find the maximum value of the expression \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). This can be done by using the trigonometric identity for the amplitude of a sinusoidal function. The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta - b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = 432\), so the maximum value is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=45910)[0m Therefore, the largest possible real part of the given expression is \(\boxed{540}\).
